## Compatibility follow-up

The Task 1 review found that the shared ticker validator had been widened for the V3 `DUAL2`
example, unintentionally changing legacy validation. The follow-up restores `_canonical_ticker()` to
its exact pre-Task-1 character set and adds `_canonical_ticker_v3()` for schema-V3-only identity,
explicit-transition, and bundle-query paths. V1/V2 membership, price-symbol loading, provenance
validation, and inferred-transition construction remain on the legacy validator. The legacy unbound
`_query_prices()` test surface also retains its original validator fallback.

Follow-up verification:

- Direct validator compatibility smoke: passed. It proved V1/V2 membership, price, and provenance
  reject digit-bearing tickers with the base error; V3 accepts `DUAL2` and resolves `DUAL -> DUAL2`;
  provenance rejects noncanonical raw case/whitespace; both validators reject unsupported `_`, `/`,
  and `:` punctuation.
- `python -B -m pytest tests/test_pit_data.py -q`: 7 passed.
- `python -B -m py_compile core/pit_data.py core/pit_universe_v3.py`: passed.
- `python -B -m ruff check core/pit_data.py core/pit_universe_v3.py`: passed.
- `git diff --check`: passed with only the Windows line-ending notice.

Follow-up commit: `c4da6a4` — `fix: isolate schema-v3 ticker validation`

## Resolver-isolation follow-up

The rereview identified one remaining content-based schema inference inside
`PriceIdentityTransitionContract.resolve_open_holding()`. The resolver no longer inspects identity
keys. The original method explicitly applies the legacy validator, while the new
`resolve_open_holding_v3()` method explicitly applies schema-V3 ticker syntax and delegates to the
same transition-resolution implementation. `PointInTimeUniverseV3.ticker_for_lineage_at()` now
routes its final identity check through the explicit V3 resolver.

Follow-up verification:

- Direct explicit-resolver smoke: passed. The same directly constructed contract rejects `DUAL2`
  through `resolve_open_holding()`, accepts it only through `resolve_open_holding_v3()`, preserves
  `DUAL -> DUAL2` on the transition date, and keeps V3 universe membership on `DUAL2` afterward.
- Both resolver surfaces rejected unsupported `_`, `/`, and `:` punctuation.
- `python -B -m pytest tests/test_pit_data.py -q`: 7 passed.
- `python -B -m py_compile core/pit_data.py core/pit_universe_v3.py`: passed.
- `python -B -m ruff check core/pit_data.py core/pit_universe_v3.py`: passed.
- `git diff --check`: passed with only the Windows line-ending notice.

Resolver-isolation commit: `2f8f84c` — `fix: make schema-v3 identity resolution explicit`
